# Model card: churn risk score

**Purpose.** Rank customers by probability of churning so a retention offer can be targeted. Not for pricing or credit decisions.

**Data.** IBM Telco Customer Churn sample, {{ a.kpi.customers | num }} customers, churn rate {{ a.kpi.churn_rate | pct }}.

## Protocol

| Item | Choice |
|---|---|
| Split | Stratified train/test, {{ p.n_train | num }} / {{ p.n_test | num }} customers, seed {{ p.seed }} (train churn {{ p.train_churn_rate | pct }}, test {{ p.test_churn_rate | pct }}) |
| Model selection | {{ p.cv_folds }}-fold stratified CV ROC-AUC on the training set only |
| Features | {{ p.n_features_raw }} raw fields: tenure, monthly and total charges, add-on count, five yes/no flags, eleven categorical fields (one-hot) |
| Excluded | {% for k, v in lk.excluded_columns.items() %}`{{ k }}` ({{ v }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} |
| Imbalance | Stratification, PR-AUC, cost-based threshold; class-weighted variant reported for comparison |
| Threshold | {{ m.threshold.chosen | sig }}, maximising campaign net value on out-of-fold training predictions |

